      "ingredients": "1 pack (500g) Pampanga’s Best Chicken Lumpiang Shanghai\n2 tbsps. vegetable oil \n2 medium carrots, diced\n1 cup leeks, thinly sliced, plus more for garnish\n3 cloves garlic, minced\n2 cups cooked day-old white rice \n3 large eggs, beaten\n2 tbsps. soy sauce\n1 tbsp. oyster sauce\n1 tsp. sesame oil\n1/4 tsp. white pepper",
      "procedure": "Cook Pampanga’s Best Chicken Lumpiang Shanghai according to the package instructions. Set aside a portion of whole pieces for topping, and chop the remaining pieces into bite-sized chunks.\nHeat vegetable oil in a large wok over medium-high heat. Add the diced carrots, and cook for about 3-4 minutes until they begin to soften. Add the sliced leeks and minced garlic, and stir-fry for another 2-3 minutes until the leeks are tender.\nAdd the cooked rice to the wok, breaking up any clumps with a spatula. Stir well to combine with the vegetables. \nMake a well in the middle of the rice, then add in the eggs. Scramble until mostly cooked through, then mix into the rice and vegetables. \nPour in the soy sauce, oyster sauce, sesame oil, and white pepper. Stir-fry for another 2-3 minutes until the rice is evenly coated.\nTo serve, top every serving of fried rice with extra whole pieces of Pampanga’s Best Chicken Lumpiang Shanghai."
